{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJy21EBmEJ1PgmzanRz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HbyReP9iSBWZA5ptMoWKuu","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-4qeQbr/memory/api-error-response-convention.md","content":"---\nname: api-error-response-convention\ndescription: Agreed API error body shape ({error:{code,message}}, UPPER_SNAKE codes) with the mobile team; legacy plain-text errors in lib/routes.js pending migration\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nEvery API error response body must be `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } }`. The `code` is upper case with underscores, e.g. `INVOICE_NOT_FOUND`.\n\nThe mobile app switches on `code` and shows `message` to the user as-is, so codes are a stable contract and messages must be user-presentable.\n\nThe plain-text errors already in `lib/routes.js` predate this convention and will be migrated separately. Don't treat them as the pattern to follow, and don't migrate them unless asked.\n\n**Why:** Agreed with the mobile team; changing a code or the body shape breaks the app.\n\n**How to apply:** Use this shape for any new or changed error response. Don't rename existing codes without checking with the mobile team.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":583,"cache_read_input_tokens":22059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":583,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":41,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52a74b92-76dd-4ed9-8223-5e37efdce258","uuid":"d264bda3-799f-483d-bf20-b12fc31cdb20","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:34:16.033Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJy1sn5JKhzLYuSy2pR","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HbyReP9iSBWZA5ptMoWKuu":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-4qeQbr/memory/api-error-response-convention.md","content":"---\nname: api-error-response-convention\ndescription: Agreed API error body shape ({error:{code,message}}, UPPER_SNAKE codes) with the mobile team; legacy plain-text errors in lib/routes.js pending migration\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nEvery API error response body must be `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } }`. The `code` is upper case with underscores, e.g. `INVOICE_NOT_FOUND`.\n\nThe mobile app switches on `code` and shows `message` to the user as-is, so codes are a stable contract and messages must be user-presentable.\n\nThe plain-text errors already in `lib/routes.js` predate this convention and will be migrated separately. Don't treat them as the pattern to follow, and don't migrate them unless asked.\n\n**Why:** Agreed with the mobile team; changing a code or the body shape breaks the app.\n\n**How to apply:** Use this shape for any new or changed error response. Don't rename existing codes without checking with the mobile team.\n"}}}
